WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:06.330
The longest novel in the world as recognized
by the Guinness Book of World Records is A

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.809
la recherché du temps perdu by Marcel Proust.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:21.200
Within its pages are an estimated 9,609,000
characters, including spaces.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.050
When classical music is played in restaurants,
people spend more money on wine.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:32.250
At his execution, Louis XVI was too fat to
fit into the guillotine.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:38.110
In 2012, the fifth-oldest tree in the world
was burned down by a crystal-meth addict.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.219
The smell of freshly cut grass is a plant
distress call.

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:46.210
When you cut the grass it is actually crying
out for help.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.710
The second episode of the The Muppets was
called 'Sex and Violence'.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.000
Diamonds can actually boil!

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.729
They have an absolute boiling point of 4300
degrees Kelvin assuming particular atmospheric

00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:01.100
conditions are met.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:07.300
There are more than 915,000,000 ways to combine
six standard Lego bricks.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:14.150
The Boy Scouts' motto 'Be prepared' was originally
followed by 'to die for your country'.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:18.940
By 2019, there will be more Lego figures on
Earth than people.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:26.450
Scientists estimate that between 1986 and
2007, humankind has gathered 295 exabytes

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.000
of data in digital storage around the world.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.740
That's 295 million terabytes!

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:39.320
But that's still less than 1% of the total
information stored in human DNA.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.600
The Royal Navy uses blasts of Britney Spears's
'Oops!

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.070
. . . I Did It Again' to scare off Somali
pirates.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:52.670
For Irish based surnames, the prefix “Mac”
means “son of”, and the prefix “O'”

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.860
means “grandson of” or “descendant of”.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.490
Rain following a dry spell is often accompanied
by a pleasant smell that permeates the air.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:07.440
That smell is known as “petrichor”, and
it's believed to be caused by organic compounds.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.000
The appropriate response to 'How are you?'
in Luxembourgish is 'Tip-Top'.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.440
Our modern word “ostracize”, which means
to “exclude (someone) from a society or

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:23.410
group” according to the Oxford Dictionary,
comes from the Ancient Greek practice of ostracism,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:28.390
where Athenians could force another of their
number into an “honorable exile” after

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:30.010
a majority vote.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:34.850
This was often used by political rivals to
literally remove their opponents from the

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:43.550
scene.

